// Natural resources and gathering (milestone 2, step 2).
// Each rule says where a good can be gathered and how much. A cell's richness for a good is the
// largest of the terms that apply to it, from 0 (none) to 1 (plenty):
//   biomes: by the cell's current biome; terrain: lowland, hills or mountains;
//   river: on any river; coast: next to the sea; dryCoast: next to the sea where rain is below
//   dryRainMm a year; dryLakeShore: next to a lake where rain is below dryRainMm; farmland:
//   where crops are farmed; sources: within sourceRadiusKm of a listed place.
// Each January the farmers of a settled cell can gather perPerson units each times richness
// into the settlement's store. They gather a good only up to what the settlement wants, and only
// if that much is worth at least gatherTimeValue at local prices (prices.json).
